msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:254
msgid "Position"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:266
msgid "Brand name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:270
msgid "Logo URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:274
msgid "Trigger selector"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:277
msgid "A CSS selector for your own button. Leave empty for the floating button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:281
msgid "Keyboard shortcut"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:284
msgid "Opens the panel from the keyboard. \"mod\" is Command on a Mac and Ctrl everywhere else. Leave empty for no shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:288
msgid "Open on error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:292
msgid "Open the panel by itself when the page throws an uncaught error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:294
msgid "Off by default: it shows the panel to whoever happens to be on the page, including customers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:298
msgid "Evidence"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:302
msgid "Breadcrumbs: record clicks, navigations and form submits before the report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:306
msgid "Network log: record requests that failed or were slow. Never their bodies or headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:311
msgid "Screenshots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:315
msgid "Let the reporter attach a picture of the page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:317
msgid "Off by default. Taking a picture needs a renderer, and a renderer is a second script of about 15 kB (6 kB over the wire) on every page the panel is on, so it is only loaded when this box is ticked. Until version 0.4.1 the plugin shipped no renderer at all and the panel never offered a picture."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:318
msgid "A picture of the page contains whatever was on the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:318
msgid "The name of another customer, a price, an order, a message that was open in a tab beside the bug. Reports are a private post type and the picture is served only to people who can read them, through a plugin route of its own rather than the media library — but everyone who can read a report sees it, and forwarding one forwards the picture. Ask for screenshots only if you would be comfortable reading them."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: the data-bugbottle-mask attribute, wrapped in <code>; 2: the data-bugbottle-block attribute, wrapped in <code>
#: includes/class-settings.php:323
#, php-format
msgid "What is typed into a field is replaced with bullets before the picture is taken. Mark anything else you do not want in it with %1$s to bullet its text, or %2$s to cover it entirely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:329
msgid "The reporter sees the picture before it is sent, can untick it, and can mark it first: a rectangle, an arrow, and a blur that reads the region back out of the canvas so the original pixels leave with it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:333
msgid "Offline queue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:337
msgid "Keep a report the browser could not send and deliver it when the connection is back"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:339
msgid "Reports wait in the browser, for up to seven days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:343
msgid "Timings and storage snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:347
msgid "Record how the page performed, and which keys the browser had stored"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:349
msgid "Off by default. The timings are the ones a web vitals report shows: largest contentful paint, layout shift, interaction to next paint, time to first byte, the load events, long tasks and — in Chrome — the JavaScript heap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:350
msgid "The storage snapshot lists the key names in localStorage and sessionStorage with the length of each value, and the names of the cookies. It never records a value, and never a cookie value at all. A key name can still say something — \"impersonating_user\" is a fact about the visit — so read the report screen before you forward one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:354
msgid "Shake to report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:358
msgid "Open the panel when the phone is shaken"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:360
msgid "Off by default. It is the gesture a phone has instead of a keyboard shortcut: three shakes inside a second, with a three-second pause afterwards so one gesture opens one panel."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the JavaScript call a theme has to make, already wrapped in <code>
#: includes/class-settings.php:365
#, php-format
msgid "On iPhone and iPad, Safari only reports motion after the visitor has agreed to it, and it will only ask from a button the visitor pressed. This plugin never puts up that prompt for you. If you want the gesture there, call %s from a button of your own; everywhere else it works as soon as you tick this box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:373
msgid "Scrubbing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:377
msgid "Redact email addresses, tokens, card numbers and query values before the report is sent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:382
msgid "Signing key(s)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:385
msgid "One key per line. A report must then arrive signed with any one of them, and a report signed with a key that is not here is refused. Several lines is how a key is rotated: add the new one, wait for cached pages carrying the old one to expire, then delete the old one. Empty means no signature is asked for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:386
msgid "A key that is sent to the browser is public."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:386
msgid "It is in the page source, so anyone who wants it has it. Signing raises the cost of sending junk to the endpoint from a script that has not read your page — it is spam deterrence beside the rate limit, and it is not authentication. Do not treat it as securing the endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-settings.php:387
msgid "The bundled panel signs what it sends, so filling this in is all there is to it. A report sent by anything else — your own form, a script — has to sign the same way."
msgstr ""

